26
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,940
And flyback, familiar.

27
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:34,480
And I've built such schematics.

28
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:36,160
Everything looks great to me.

29
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:39,160
This pulse — we'll flip it now and you won't see it there.

30
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:40,820
It's only here at this point.

31
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,420
So — measurement 1.

32
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:45,220
Confirming that my probes are still intact.

33
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:49,520
Oscilloscope common is on minus.

34
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:55,460
Now we'll watch the oscillogram on the transistor gates.

35
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:57,140
That is, after the drivers.

36
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:01,620
Here — two probes, and you can see the picture is identical.

37
00:02:02,020 --> 00:02:02,960
There, damn, it works.

38
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:07,260
Potential is 15 volts.

39
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:10,040
And here we see power.

40
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:15,040
Exactly 15 volts, drawing 0.15 A.

41
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,680
Probes normal — passed the check.

42
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:28,140
So, now the probe has moved — also relative to common minus — to the output of one of the bifilars.

43
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:33,160
I do all measurements directly before the diode, not after it.

44
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,740
After it is useless — there's DC on the cap.

45
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,480
So strictly before the diode.

46
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:45,460
Now applying — voltage isn't applied to the switches yet, here's the oscillogram, applying voltage.

47
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:51,260
Remember, we have this kind of oscillogram.

48
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,460
Here it is.

49
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,800
Remember it well.

50
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,400
It's not back EMF.

51
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:07,520
Now look — switching common to plus.

52
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:09,080
Switched.

53
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:12,020
The oscillogram is still there.

54
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:13,400
Here it is.

55
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,920
Now look — even a joke.

56
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,760
Measurements aren't done this way, but watch — I'll disconnect common.

57
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,900
Only the probe hangs.

58
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:25,780
Positive.

59
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:27,980
The oscillogram is still there.

60
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:32,960
This current doesn't belong to this system, to the power source.

61
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,520
Now switching the probe.

62
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:39,360
Look on the contrary.

63
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,840
You won't see this signal there — none of it at that point.

64
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,880
Probe flipped.

65
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,940
Now it's on minus of power.

66
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,800
Common on the same bifilar.

67
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,580
Here's the picture.

68
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,300
No flipped signal of large amplitude that we saw before.

69
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,700
