70
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:02,520
Now 20 V per cell.

71
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:03,800
None of that signal.

72
00:04:05,140 --> 00:04:09,620
Now switching the probe to plus.

73
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:12,800
I don't see anything in this sense, but let me switch it.

74
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:13,980
Here it is on plus.

75
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:18,120
Here's the work.

76
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:19,940
None of that signal.

77
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,940
It's only in one place.

78
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:28,880
Swap places — everything's as it should be.

79
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:34,460
Place the probe.

80
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,540
Didn't even connect it yet.

81
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:42,540
Look — we need to change the volts-per-cell sweep.

82
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:44,340
Amplitude is very high here.

83
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:51,500
Going to have to change it because we won't see.

84
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,300
Here's the oscillogram.

85
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:03,260
No matter what we measure relative to what, I already showed.

86
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,080
Place it relative to plus here.

87
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:08,200
Signal remains.

88
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:10,020
Don't change any settings.

89
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:16,500
And relative to minus — also don't change any settings.

90
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,100
Signal remains.

91
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:22,180
Swap this probe around.

92
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:30,760
No point — because we need this effect specifically at this point, where the break happens at the switch.

93
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,520
Let's do the next measurement.

94
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:37,780
The yellow channel will hang on one of the bifilars as before.

95
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:42,720
