104
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,260
DC.

105
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:15,220
Sweep is 10 V per cell.

106
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:22,140
Now it makes a bit more than one cell.

107
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:25,320
And the voltage is exactly 17 V here.

108
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,140
Everything matches.

109
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,660
Apply higher — this potential grows.

110
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:36,040
And on the yellow channel we have a sweep — here it is, 50 V per cell.

111
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:43,640
That is, we see a classical normal measurement relative to the common point.

112
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:50,140
Actually DC — here it is, watch the blue channel.

113
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:51,300
DC.

114
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:57,700
One more thing — maybe DC doesn't go to the lamp.

115
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:00,860
Let's measure on the lamp too — does DC go there.

116
