Here I connected the lamp — in that case we looked at 100 W, here I found 200 W.

117
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:12,780
Got 200 W on it.

118
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:18,620
Here you see the output and we measure directly — here the probe is on the lamp.

119
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:23,000
Look — applying voltage, lamp lights up, watch.

120
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:32,860
Apply — you see potential growing on the lamp, DC, no sags, nothing.

121
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:37,960
Watch — the lamp's running at the output, hanging there.

122
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,700
Measurement done strictly on DC.

123
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:46,860
If that weren't the case, I wouldn't post the measurement and calculate efficiency.

124
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,140
It all works.

125
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:58,500
So don't make stuff up — if you don't know how to measure, I like how I measure, measure yourself.

126
